course: dictionary
lesson: 7380
title: One word, many meanings: pluck
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: One word can have several meanings, and the context tells you which one is meant. Pluck is a good example. «The guzheng is a Chinese plucked zither» uses plucked for playing strings. Ask yourself what would fit: pull the strings with your fingers makes sense for an instrument.
explain: Look at the words around the word. In the French song «Alouette», each verse says je te plumerai, which means "I will pluck your feathers." The clues are feathers, a lark and body parts, so pluck means pull the feathers off. The tune itself is not the clue.
explain: Pluck can also be a noun meaning courage. Try this sentence: «It took a lot of pluck to stand up and speak.» Swap in courage and check: "It took a lot of courage to stand up and speak" still makes sense, so pluck means courage here.
fact: Pluck is a verb and a noun. As a verb it means to pull something off or out quickly.
fact: As a verb, pluck can mean to pull the feathers off a bird before cooking, or to pull and let go of a guitar or harp string with your fingers.
fact: As a noun, pluck means courage and spirit in a difficult situation: «a lot of pluck».
fact: «Pluck up the courage» means to make yourself brave enough to do something.
fact: The guzheng is a plucked Chinese zither, played in China for over 2,000 years.
exercise: «She had to pluck up the courage to speak.» What does pluck up the courage mean? | *Make yourself brave enough to do something | Play a tune on a guitar | Pull a flower out of the ground | Pull the feathers off a bird
exercise: «The harpist gently plucked a string, and a clear note rang out.» What does plucked mean here? | Tied tightly in a knot | Pulled out quickly, like a weed | Pulled the feathers off a bird before cooking | *Pulled and let go of a string with the fingers
exercise: Which sentence uses pluck to mean courage? | The chef plucked the chicken for dinner | He plucked his guitar all evening | *The little boy showed real pluck when the dog barked | She plucked daisies from the lawn
test: «The guzheng is a Chinese plucked zither.» What does plucked mean here? | Painted in bright colours | Cut into small pieces | *Played by pulling the strings with the fingers | Pulled the feathers from a bird
test: Pluck can be a verb or a noun. As a noun, what does pluck mean? | A type of feather | Pulling something out quickly | *Courage and spirit in a difficult situation | One string on a harp
exam: Which meaning fits «She plucked up the courage to sing a solo»? | To hide quietly | *To make herself brave enough to do something | To tune a guitar | To pull out feathers
